  "notes": {
    "heritage": "The EJ207 is the most celebrated engine in Subaru's history. Born from WRC homologation requirements, it powered Subaru to three consecutive Manufacturers' Championships (1995-1997) and multiple Drivers' titles.",
    "jdm_only": "The EJ207 was only available in Japan. USDM STI models received the EJ257 2.5L instead.",
    "high_revving": "Unlike the torque-focused EJ257, the EJ207 is designed for high RPM power. The 8000+ RPM redline and characteristic boxer rumble define the driving experience.",
    "wrc_lineage": "Rally-derived technologies include semi-closed deck blocks, sodium-filled exhaust valves, and DCCD center differentials.",
